    "title": "Why Chile Is So Long & So Thin 🇨🇱🤯 4,300 km Ribbon Country",
    "description": "Chile 🇨🇱 is about 4,300 km long but on average only 177 km wide 📏 Why? To the east, the Andes form a giant wall ⛰️ and to the west there's only the Pacific Ocean 🌊 In the War of the Pacific (1879–1884) Chile defeated Bolivia 🇧🇴 and Peru 🇵🇪 and expanded its territory northward by almost one-third, taking the nitrate-rich Atacama and leaving Bolivia without a coast. That's how Chile became a ribbon squeezed between mountains and ocean 🤯",
